@knowledge adoc_hub
@viewpoints specification
@description {
  The adoc hub, a herdr-ranch plugin that shows every adoc on the ranch network in one browser: it finds the adoc servers on each machine, routes a browser at one central address to each of them, and lets a person approve browsers and name hosts.
}
@scope {
  Cover the plugin server and the persistent clients, how a client finds the adoc servers of its machine, the hosts and their names, the routing client of a machine, the tunnel between client and server, the discovery list, the remapping of each host under the hub's address, browser approval, the status screen and the name command.
  Exclude the adoc web UI itself, which belongs to adoc and adoc_ui, and the ranch network, which belongs to herdr-ranch.
}

concept _Adoc_Hub_ in hub = {
  The herdr-ranch plugin `adoc-hub`, written in Rust and kept in the adoc repository under `ranch-plugin/`, made of one _Hub_Server_ and one _Hub_Client_ in every herdr session on the ranch network.
.relations
  has_part _Hub_Server_
  has_part _Hub_Client_
  serves _Hub_Host_
.contract
  - The _Adoc_Hub_ must follow the plugin contract of herdr-ranch: a `herdr-plugin.toml` and a `ranch.toml`, GitHub releases with a `.sha256` per asset, a server built for the central machine (Linux x86_64, glibc 2.36 or static), and a persistent client that re-executes itself on `plugin_updated`.
  - The _Adoc_Hub_ must learn agents, their status and the clients of each session from the ranch Directory, never by finding them itself.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the layout of herdr-connect, one crate whose binary holds the server, the client with its pane, and the command line.
}

concept _Hub_Server_ in hub = {
  The plugin server of the _Adoc_Hub_, one on the central machine of the ranch network, that keeps the list of hosts, picks the _Routing_Client_ of each machine, owns the tunnels and serves browsers.
.relations
  part of _Adoc_Hub_
  keeps _Hub_Host_
  picks _Routing_Client_
  ends _Hub_Tunnel_
  serves _Hub_Discovery_
  serves _Hub_Remap_
  grants _Browser_Approval_
  stores _Hub_Host_Name_
.contract
  - The _Hub_Server_ must listen for browsers on its exposed port `web` and for tunnels on a port forwarded to every machine as `tunnel`.
  - The _Hub_Server_ must keep its state, the host names and the approved browsers, in `RANCH_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR`, written atomically.
  - The _Hub_Server_ must answer every browser request without an approved browser cookie with the approval page of _Browser_Approval_, except the approval requests themselves.
}

concept _Hub_Client_ in hub = {
  The persistent client of the _Adoc_Hub_ in one herdr session, which reports the adoc servers of its machine, carries tunnels to them when it is the _Routing_Client_, and draws the _Hub_Status_Screen_ in the plugin pane.
.relations
  references _adoc_hub:Hub_Server_
  references _adoc_hub:Routing_Client_
  part of _Adoc_Hub_
  runs _Local_Discovery_
  opens _Hub_Tunnel_
  draws _Hub_Status_Screen_
.contract
  - A _Hub_Client_ picked as the _Routing_Client_ of its machine must report the result of _Local_Discovery_ to the _Hub_Server_ by datagram when it is picked and whenever the result changes.
  - A _Hub_Client_ must reach adoc servers only on their loopback URLs on its own machine.
  - A _Hub_Client_ must connect again after a ranch network disconnect and report again after the next welcome, since datagrams are never replayed.
}

procedure _Local_Discovery_ in hub = {
  How a _Hub_Client_ finds the adoc servers of its machine: by running `adoc server list --output json` every few seconds.
.relations
  references _adoc_hub:Hub_Status_Screen_
  run by _Hub_Client_
  invokes _adoc:Server_List_Command_
  produces _Hub_Host_
.contract
  - _Local_Discovery_ must take the servers only from the JSON of the _adoc:Server_List_Command_, with their workspace, URL, process id and online or offline status, never from the server record files.
  - _Local_Discovery_ must find the `adoc` program in this order: the path set by `ADOC_BIN`, the programs on `PATH`, then the path that the user's login shell reports for `adoc`; when none is found, the _Hub_Status_Screen_ must say so.
  - For each online server, _Local_Discovery_ must add the server's name, version and assigned agent from its `/api/workspace`.
.remarks
  - Chosen: herdr runs plugins without the user's login shell, so an `adoc` installed by npm under nvm is usually not on their `PATH`; the login shell finds it as the user's terminal does.
  - Chosen: the command rather than the record files, because the files may change place or shape; adoc owns them.
}

concept _Hub_Host_ in hub = {
  One adoc workspace as the _Adoc_Hub_ sees it: the machine, the workspace path, the URL and port of its server, whether it is online or offline, and its assigned agent, addressed in the hub by its _Hub_Host_Name_ or by `<machine>_<port>`.
.relations
  references _adoc:Server_List_Command_
  references _adoc_hub:Adoc_Hub_
  produced by _Local_Discovery_
  named by _Hub_Host_Name_
  routed by _Routing_Client_
  listed by _Hub_Discovery_
.contract
  - A _Hub_Host_ must be identified by its machine and workspace path; its address `<machine>_<port>` follows the port of its server, its name does not.
  - A _Hub_Host_ must stay in the list as offline while its server record stays, and leave the list when the record leaves the _adoc:Server_List_Command_.
  - The status of the assigned agent of a _Hub_Host_ must come from the ranch Directory entry of the pane its server reports as claimed.
}

concept _Hub_Host_Name_ in hub = {
  The name a person or an agent gives a _Hub_Host_, kept by the _Hub_Server_ for its machine and workspace path, so that the host keeps one address across restarts and port changes.
.relations
  names _Hub_Host_
  stored by _Hub_Server_
  set by _Hub_Status_Screen_
  set by _Hub_Name_Command_
.contract
  - A _Hub_Host_Name_ must be unique on the hub, made of lowercase letters, digits and `-`, and must not have the form `<machine>_<port>`.
  - A named _Hub_Host_ must answer at both its name and its `<machine>_<port>` address.
}

concept _Routing_Client_ in hub = {
  The one _Hub_Client_ of a machine that the _Hub_Server_ picks to report and carry the hosts of that machine, when several herdr sessions on it run a _Hub_Client_.
.relations
  references _adoc_hub:Hub_Client_
  picked by _Hub_Server_
  routes _Hub_Host_
  opens _Hub_Tunnel_
.contract
  - The _Hub_Server_ must pick a _Routing_Client_ for a machine when the first _Hub_Client_ of that machine connects, and must tell it by datagram.
  - When the _Routing_Client_ leaves, the _Hub_Server_ must pick another connected _Hub_Client_ of the same machine, if any; until one is picked, the hosts of that machine are shown as unreachable.
  - Only the _Routing_Client_ of a machine reports and carries its hosts; the reports of other clients of that machine are ignored.
}

concept _Hub_Tunnel_ in hub = {
  The WebSocket that a _Routing_Client_ opens to the _Hub_Server_ through the forwarded port `tunnel`, over which many HTTP requests and WebSockets between browsers and the adoc servers of its machine travel as numbered streams.
.relations
  opened by _Routing_Client_
  ended by _Hub_Server_
  carries _Hub_Remap_
.contract
  - A _Routing_Client_ must open its _Hub_Tunnel_ when the _Hub_Server_ asks by datagram, and must open it again after it drops.
  - A _Hub_Tunnel_ must carry each HTTP request and each WebSocket as its own stream, so that a slow stream, such as a large asset, does not hold back another, such as terminal frames.
  - Datagrams must carry only signals and reports; every byte of a request or a WebSocket must travel through the _Hub_Tunnel_.
.remarks
  - Chosen: one connection per machine, opened from the machine to the central server, so that adoc servers stay on loopback and no machine needs to accept connections.
}

concept _Hub_Discovery_ in hub = {
  The list of every _Hub_Host_ that the _Hub_Server_ serves at `/adoc-discovery`, read by the host switcher of the adoc web UI.
.relations
  served by _Hub_Server_
  lists _Hub_Host_
  read by _adoc_ui:Host_Switcher_
.contract
  - `GET /adoc-discovery` must return, for each _Hub_Host_, its address, name, machine, workspace path, online or offline, adoc version, and the name and status of its assigned agent.
  - The _Hub_Discovery_ must offer the same list as a stream of changes, so that a browser follows hosts and agent status without polling.
  - The shape of the _Hub_Discovery_ is a contract between the hub and every adoc version; it may only grow.
}

concept _Hub_Remap_ in hub = {
  The rule by which the _Hub_Server_ serves each _Hub_Host_ under its own address: `/<host>/…` goes to the server of that host as `/…`.
.relations
  references _adoc_hub:Hub_Host_
  served by _Hub_Server_
  carried by _Hub_Tunnel_
  sets _adoc:Web_UI_Base_
.contract
  - The _Hub_Server_ must forward a request for `/<host>/<path>` to that host's server as `/<path>`, with `X-Forwarded-Prefix: /<host>` and `X-Adoc-Hub: /adoc-discovery`, and must forward WebSocket upgrades the same way.
  - The _Hub_Server_ must pass the pages, scripts and responses of each host unchanged, so that every host serves its own adoc version.
  - A request for an offline or unknown host must get a page saying so, with a link to the list.
}

concept _Browser_Approval_ in hub = {
  How a browser gets access to the _Hub_Server_: it shows a short code, every _Hub_Status_Screen_ shows the same request, and a person approves or rejects it in any herdr session.
.relations
  references _adoc_hub:Hub_Client_
  granted by _Hub_Server_
  decided on _Hub_Status_Screen_
.contract
  - A browser without an approved cookie must get a page showing a short code and waiting; the _Hub_Server_ must send the request, with the code, the browser's address and its user agent, to every _Hub_Client_.
  - When a person approves the request on any _Hub_Status_Screen_, the waiting browser must get a long-lived cookie and continue; a rejection must end the request; the other screens must drop it.
  - A code must be valid for one request and expire after a few minutes.
  - The _Hub_Server_ must keep only a hash of each approved cookie, and the _Hub_Status_Screen_ must be able to revoke an approved browser.
.remarks
  - Chosen: whoever can type in a herdr pane on the ranch network can approve, which is the trust the network already gives.
}

concept _Hub_Status_Screen_ in hub = {
  The screen that a _Hub_Client_ draws in the plugin pane that ranch keeps open in every herdr session: the hosts with their state, the names to give them, and the browsers waiting for approval.
.relations
  references _adoc_hub:Hub_Host_
  drawn by _Hub_Client_
  decides _Browser_Approval_
  sets _Hub_Host_Name_
.contract
  - The _Hub_Status_Screen_ must list every _Hub_Host_ of the hub with its address, name, online or offline and agent status, and mark the hosts of its own machine.
  - The _Hub_Status_Screen_ must show each waiting _Browser_Approval_ with its code, and must let the person approve or reject it with single keys.
  - The _Hub_Status_Screen_ must let the person give, change or remove the _Hub_Host_Name_ of a host.
.remarks
  - Chosen: no settings screen; the hub has nothing to configure.
}

procedure _Hub_Name_Command_ in hub = {
  The command `adoc-hub name <name>`, which an agent or a person runs in an adoc workspace to give its _Hub_Host_ a _Hub_Host_Name_; `adoc-hub name --clear` removes it.
.relations
  references _adoc_hub:Hub_Client_
  references _adoc_hub:Hub_Server_
  sets _Hub_Host_Name_
  references _Hub_Host_
.contract
  - The _Hub_Name_Command_ must find the _Hub_Host_ of the adoc workspace containing the current directory, send the name to the _Hub_Server_ through the _Hub_Client_ of its session, and print the result or the reason for a refusal.
}
